      "id": 1,
      "text": "Reston was founded in 1964, inspired by the Garden City movement that blended green space with residential and commercial areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reston%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Reston Historic Trust & Museum, the town’s sole museum, sits in Lake Anne Plaza and chronicles the community’s evolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reston%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Reston Black Focus, established in 1969, emerged to champion Black community interests in education, politics, and culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.restonmuseum.org/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Reston Community Players, originally the Reston Players, have staged productions at Hunters Woods Plaza since 1966.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reston%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2014, the Metro Silver Line opened its first Reston station, Wiehle‑Reston East, linking the town to Washington, D.C.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reston%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Greater Reston Arts Center, founded by local artists, hosts the annual Northern Virginia Fine Arts Festival at Reston Town Center.",
